[# Living decision log + open-issue tracker for the CX language project.
   Updated with every architectural decision. CX-shaped so it is queryable
   once the evaluator supports the v0.8.0 surface (post ADR 0028). Numbered
   ids stay stable across edits — use the &id form on every decision so
   cross-refs from ADRs and conversations land on a permanent anchor.

   Lifecycle:
     decisions  →  append-only; status moves accepted → revisited → superseded
                   but the entry remains in place.
     open       →  one entry per blocked / pending issue; linked to its
                   blocking ADR via :blocks-on.
     adrs       →  the ADR register; one row per draft / proposed / accepted /
                   superseded ADR; dep graph via :builds-on.
     completed  →  moved here from `open` when fully done + verified
                   (not merely merged). #]

[backlog

  [meta
    title='CX Language Backlog'
    last-updated=2026-05-22T20:00
    branch=v0.8.0-dev
    rendered-form='docs/internal/backlog.md (deferred — render after ADR 0028)']

  [- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     DECISIONS — append-only; date-ordered.
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -]

  [decisions

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-01
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Brand: CX is data and code, not data and programs'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Reads more naturally; "programs" carries imperative
        connotation that conflicts with CX's pure functional model. "Code"
        is the standard pairing with "data" in industry vernacular.'''
      :scope brand-and-docs
      :applies-to '[docs-src/, READMEs, taglines, public-facing surface]'
      :defers 'internal API rename (cx_code_eval, vcx/code/, code.md) — separate ADR; cascades through every binding']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-02
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'ADR-first design workflow'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Encode considered-alternatives + rationale in ADRs
        alongside the decision; design conversations do not recur.
        Implementation PRs cite the ratified ADR.'''
      :applies-to 'every architectural change for v0.8.0 forward']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-03
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Reduce binding set for v0.8.0 — V (native) + Python + Go + Rust'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Concurrent maintenance for 10 bindings prevents
        validation of design choices; 4 covers static/dynamic ×
        compiled/interpreted spectrum. Drift sources during v0.7.6
        (TS GC, Rust ABI catchup, Python decoder ceiling) all
        consumed Tier-1 design time.'''
      :archived '[typescript, java, csharp, ruby, kotlin, swift]'
      :archive-location 'lang/_archived/<lang>/ — preserves history; not deleted'
      :restoration 'opt-in once Layer-1 method set is stable; community contributions accepted but not blocked on']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-04
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Skip v0.7.6 tag; go v0.7.5 → v0.8.0'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''v0.7.6-dev surface has open design gaps (CXPath
        retired with no terse replacement; no multi-arm match; no
        modify directive; doc-gen sectional regression). Tagging
        would commit to a surface immediately superseded.'''
      :preservation 'v0.7.6-dev work carries forward on v0.8.0-dev branch (not deleted, just untagged)']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-05
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Single guide: cx-data-and-code-guide — multi-file CX source'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Authoring in CX (eats own dog food); rendering to MD
        deferred until evaluator supports sectional structure
        (post ADR 0028). One canonical guide reduces decision cost for
        readers; numbered section refs (1.2.3) provide stable anchors
        for PR diffs and cross-references.'''
      :source 'docs-src/canonical/sections/*.cxd + manifest.cxd + template.cx'
      :artifact 'docs/cx-data-and-code-guide.md (post v0.8.0)'
      :overflow-policy 'normative depth lives in spec/*.md; the guide curates the learning + reference path']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-06
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Public docs (GitHub Pages) stay on v0.7.5 until v0.8.0 ships'
      :status accepted
      :rationale 'docs/ tree is unchanged from v0.7.5 (verified byte-identical). Do NOT run make docs-publish on v0.8.0-dev until the design ADRs ratify and sectional rendering works.'
      :enforcement 'docs-publish target gated on a CI check that fails on v0.8.0-dev']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-07
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Layer-1 + Layer-2 binding model'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Two audiences cannot share one binding shape: CX-native
        devs want CX vocabulary; host-native devs want host idioms.
        Resolution: Layer 1 mirrors CX (identical across all bindings,
        conformance-validated); Layer 2 is per-language idiom pack
        opt-in (Pythonic / Go / Rust / etc) that desugars to Layer 1.
        CXPath strings + data-bin bytes are the bridges.'''
      :builds-on adr-0028
      :validation 'binding-API parity fixtures separate from code.txt']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-08
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Pure functional updates with lens semantics for CRUD'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Scala/Clojure/Haskell pattern — every modification
        returns a new document; structural sharing for perf;
        parallelism free by construction. CXPath identifies positions
        for both reading and writing — one selector vocabulary serves
        both directions.'''
      :builds-on '[adr-0028, adr-0030, adr-0031]'
      :rejects '[xquery-update-pending-list-semantics, sql-in-place-mutation]']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-09
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'CXPath aligns with XPath 3.1 selection core, not v0.7.0 subset'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''XPath 3.1 is the live W3C standard; users coming
        from the broader XML ecosystem know it. v0.7.0 CXPath was a
        bespoke subset with no installed base worth preserving over
        industry familiarity. Forward-looking alignment with
        documented divergences (non-duplication, safety-over-XPath-
        gotchas, XPath-4.0-watch) is the deliberate choice.'''
      :supersedes-clause 'd-2026-05-22-01 D2 narrow framing (v0.7.0 subset)'
      :divergences '[
        (no-construct-duplication: for/let/if/function delegated to CX code),
        (value-comparison-only: replaces XPath general/value dual system on = != <),
        (cx-type-vocabulary: replaces xs:integer/xs:string/etc),
        (no-expression-namespace-decls: ns declarations live in data)]'
      :verification 'gate 28.5 — reference comparison against Saxon-HE 11.x per fixture']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-10
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Retire [?find] in favor of [?for] pattern-generator + Path values'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''With Path as a value kind (ADR 0028), the search
        case has the terse spelling //pattern; the binding-capture
        case is covered by [?for [pattern] :yield expr] (code.md
        §7.5 pattern-generator). [?find] was always sugar for the
        latter (spec said so); three spellings of two operations
        breaks the unified-vocabulary discipline.'''
      :decided-in adr-0028
      :migration 'mechanical — replace [?find with [?for in every fixture and example'
      :scope '~15 fixtures, ~30 lines spec/code.md, vcx/code/tokens.v directive_names']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-11
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'ADR convention: TL;DR + syntax-at-a-glance table at top'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''ADRs are difficult to review at length; reviewers
        need a 30-second scan to decide if they want to dig into the
        rationale. Every ADR opens with: (1) TL;DR of 3-8 bullets
        listing what changes; (2) syntax-comparison tables showing
        was vs is for every shape the ADR covers; (3) then the
        existing structure (status / context / decision / D-sections /
        gates / alternatives).'''
      :applies-to 'every ADR drafted v0.8.0 forward, retrofitted to 0028 + 0029'
      :rationale-from 'reviewer feedback (user) 2026-05-22 PM']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-12
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'No keyword-comparison synonyms in CXPath; sigils only'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Sigils = != < <= > >= are the only comparison
        operators. Keyword forms eq/ne/lt/le/gt/ge are NOT in the
        grammar. Two ways to spell the same operation is language
        bloat; sigils are what XPath/SQL/everything else uses in
        practice. Value-comparison semantics (per ADR 0028 D3) apply
        to the sigils.'''
      :applies-to 'adr-0028 D3 (revised in this commit) — synonym table dropped'
      :rationale-from 'reviewer feedback (user) 2026-05-22 PM']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-13
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'ADR length discipline: cut prose to was-vs-is'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''ADRs should be scannable in 2-3 minutes top to
        bottom, not 10-15. Cut rationale to one-line claims; rely on
        the was-vs-is tables for substance; drop "Discussion" sections
        (move to backlog.cx if needed). Each D-section is one rule
        plus one-line why, not multi-paragraph essay.'''
      :applies-to 'adrs 0028 + 0029 rewritten in this commit; all future ADRs'
      :target-length '200-300 lines per ADR (down from 500+)'
      :rationale-from 'reviewer feedback (user) 2026-05-22 PM']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-14
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title '[?modify] — pure-functional updates with CXPath focus + action vocabulary'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''CRUD completion for CX code: C=element construction, R=CXPath/[?for],
        U/D=[?modify]. Lens pattern (Clojure assoc-in / Haskell lens) is the correct
        resolution: name the focus and the action separately. Original unchanged;
        structural sharing for perf. XQuery update facility (implicit pending-update-list)
        rejected as order-dependent and non-homoiconic.'''
      :decided-in adr-0030
      :action-vocabulary '[:set, :delete, :using, :rename, :set-attr, :delete-attr,
        :append, :prepend, :insert-before, :insert-after, :replace]'
      :composition 'pipeline via | for multi-step document updates'
      :perf-contract 'structural sharing: < 1 KB new heap per matched node on 10 MB doc (gate 30.5)']

    [decision &d-2026-05-22-15
      :date 2026-05-22
      :title 'Two-layer binding model — Layer 1 canonical + Layer 2 host idioms — normative in spec/bindings.md'
      :status accepted
      :rationale '''Two audiences cannot share one surface. CX-native developers
        want CX vocabulary in every host (Layer 1: identical method names and
        semantics across V/Python/Go/Rust, conformance-validated). Host-native
        developers want their language idioms (Layer 2: Pythonic comprehensions,
        Go filter chains, Rust iterator combinators — all desugar to Layer 1).
        CXPath strings + data-bin bytes are the two bridges. Layer 1 is the
        binding parity contract (conformance/binding_api.txt, gate 28.6); Layer 2
        is binding-private sugar tested via its Layer-1 desugaring.'''
      :spec spec/bindings.md
      :layer-1-method-count 16
      :layer-1-methods '[parse, bytes, hash, equals, eval, select_all, select,
        modify, find_all, root, name, attr, attrs, children, body, kind]'
      :builds-on '[d-2026-05-22-07, adr-0028]'
      :gate 'binding-api-parity (gate 28.6) — byte-identical Layer-1 results across
        V/Python/Go/Rust on conformance/binding_api.txt']]

